 {"term": "Oral Torah", "def": "In Jewish belief, the teaching given with the written Torah and handed down by word of mouth, later written in the Mishnah and Talmud."},
 {"term": "Peshat", "def": "In Jewish interpretation, the plain meaning of a verse."},
 {"term": "Midrash", "def": "Jewish interpretation of Scripture that searches out further meanings, often through stories and questions."},
 {"term": "Reader-response criticism", "def": "The modern view that meaning is made by readers, not simply found in texts."},
 {"term": "Rule of faith", "def": "The early Church's short summary of its belief, used as a guide for reading Scripture."},
 {"term": "Shema", "def": "'Hear': Deuteronomy 6:4–9, the Jewish confession of faith said morning and evening."},
